\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The two reactive families: (left) the catch schedules of the surplus-proportional Family A (\(C = \phi \,g(S)\), \(\phi = 0.25, 0.50, 0.75\)) against the flat 60-kt cap, showing that the rule harvests less than the cap near the LRP while scaling with the surplus; (right) the catch schedules of the graded Family B (graded2 and graded3) against the flat 60-kt cap. Both families vanish at or below the LRP. The dominated surplus-harvest (\(\alpha \cdot \qopname  \relax m{max}(0,g(S)-g(K^{\ast }))\)) and reactive-ramp designs are recorded in the rejected-designs note following Definition 2.4 and not plotted.\relax }}{11}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
