\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The closed loop's slope \(F'(S)\); the map is expansive at the LRP and contracts only above \(K/2 = 2500\) kt. The expansion classification is not an artifact of the particular pinned value: the grid of Section 3.7 shows \(F' \ge 1.000\) at every admissible \(K \ge 2K^* = 1769.2\) kt. The classification is conditional on \(K \ge 2K^*\): contraction (\(F' = 0.61\)--\(0.93\)) is restored only below \(2K^*\) --- exactly where the informative certificates of Sections 3.2--3.3 collapse and the fit cost rises --- and the residual bootstrap of Section 3.10 gives \(F'\) a \(90\%\) interval of \([1.010, 1.179]\).\relax }}{12}{figure.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
